---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Lumen handles data: on-device processing, explicit consent, no sharing without permission."
>
  <div class="hero">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This page explains in plain language how Lumen handles your data. It does not replace a
      complete legal notice.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="notice">
      This is a plain-language summary, not a legal document. A complete, GDPR-compliant privacy
      notice is under legal review and will be published separately before any public release of
      the app.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>On-device processing</h2>
    <p>
      Lumen's essential features run entirely on the phone, with no network connection. No audio or
      image captured by the camera or microphone ever leaves the device unless you explicitly choose
      to share it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Explicit consent</h2>
    <p>
      Any feature that shares data, for example with a family member or caregiver through the
      Famiglia module, requires explicit consent that can be revoked at any time. Face recognition
      in the Ricordare module, once available, will only work with the explicit consent of the
      people recognized, and only on-device.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Optional server</h2>
    <p>
      An optional server (<a href="https://github.com/lumen-assistive/lumen-server"
        >lumen-server</a
      >) lets caregivers sync, only if turned on voluntarily. Data sent to the server is encrypted
      before it leaves the device: the server cannot read its contents.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Medical and emergency data</h2>
    <p>
      Lumen's medical and emergency features are a support, not a replacement for a doctor or the
      112 emergency number, and Lumen is not a certified medical device.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
